  "notes": "The one rap genre at trap tempo that never drops to half-time: the snare stays hard on 2 and 4 while the kick bounces through the a-slots, so the beat walks instead of looming. Hats are eighths and deliberately full of holes. The 808 is punchy and sits still — it doubles the kick and stays on its root, which is the exact opposite of a drill slide — while a separate walking bass moves underneath. On top go jaunty off-kilter piano stabs, staccato, chromatic to the point of comedy: this is the highest half-step share in the dataset, and it is the joke the whole style is built on.",
